/*****************************************************************************
    jitXor -- IS `OR` JITTABLE? 2026-08-08. The sibling of jitXand2, which
    exits 139 on plain field operands with no degrade line at all.

    genKantParse's ALTERNATION template is an OR chain exactly as its SEQUENCE
    template is an AND chain, so the two need separate answers.

    ⚠ THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS FIXTURE WAS NON-DISCRIMINATING and is recorded
    here rather than quietly fixed: its two fires were `0 OR 1` and `1 OR 1`,
    both 1, so a folded constant would have passed it. Anti-vacuity rule --
    pair every row with a sibling that must differ.

        fire 1  0 OR 0  ->  0
        fire 2  1 OR 0  ->  1     NO RECOMPILE, and it must differ from fire 1

    exit 0 + the two answers differing  ->  OR is emitted and runs per fire
    exit 0 + both answers 0             ->  folded, or ran at emit time
    139                                 ->  OR joins AND as unjittable
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitXor);
define
    xoL;
    xoR;
    xoOut;
    xoDriver code={
        xoOut = xoL OR xoR;
        };
    ;

xoL = 0; xoR = 0; xoOut = 9;
print "XO fire 1 setup : xoL =" xoL " xoR =" xoR:;
testing(xoDriver);
print "XO fire 1 result: xoOut =" xoOut " (want 0)":;

xoL = 1; xoR = 0;
print "XO fire 2 setup : xoL =" xoL " xoR =" xoR " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "XO fire 2 result: xoOut =" xoOut " (want 1 -- MUST differ from fire 1)":;

xoL = 0; xoR = 0; xoOut = 9;
xoDriver();
print "XO interpreted  : xoOut =" xoOut " (the oracle -- want 0)":;

print "XO SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
